//FBSAANNpt Specification (prompts):
Codex App GPT-6.0:

---
update the benchmark script to support independent dataset batch sizes (DATASET_BATCH_SIZES).
set benchmark batchsize higgs=8192 (instead of 128).
update the benchmark script to support existing raw data folder (raw-data-dir).
patch benchmark script to print correct labels (backprop/fbsa).
optimise the fbsaOptimiseTrainingIterations convergence loaders to use batched data loading and the configured workers, for both backprop and FBSA.
patch option trainSetLossOptimisation=False - as per the specification, when trainSetLossOptimisation = False use validation set for training iterations optimisation only.
update the benchmark with an optional learning-rate flag.

---
upgrade the FBSAANN code to support option fbsaOptimiseTrainingIterations=True (based on LREANNpt option populationPertubationOptimiseTrainingIterations). Ensure to support both trainSetLossOptimisation = True and False (ie use validation set for training iterations optimisation).
	see the LREANNpt repo code for reference
	Please try and use the same LREANNpt populationPertubationOptimiseTrainingIterations code if possible.
upgrade your benchmark code to support option fbsaOptimiseTrainingIterations=True
	It may be simple to upgrade the benchmark_fbsaann.py to execute the FBSA codebase using optionfbsaOptimiseTrainingIterations=True instead of optionfbsaOptimiseTrainingIterations=False.
	For reference, LREANNpt used independent benchmark code to implement its option populationPertubationOptimiseTrainingIterations. An independent benchmark implementation should not be required however.

---
upgrade your implementation according to the latest PNAS 2006 version; 
https://chatgpt.com/share/6acc76d0-fb70-83ec-92c5-68ba97993273
Latest implementation (PNAS 2026):
- GitHub repository: https://github.com/liaoq/SAM2026
- Main Python implementation: https://github.com/liaoq/SAM2026/blob/main/run_netv_compare_with_bp.py
- Earlier 2024/2025 implementation: https://github.com/liaoq/SAM2026/tree/main/code_2025

---
implement option useAlgorithmFBSAANN:useFBSA=True within FBSAANNpt\_FBSAANN\_globalDefs.py/FBSAANNpt\_FBSAANN.py/FBSAANNpt\_FBSAANNmodel.py

The implementation should follow;
[https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.20018](https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.20018)
Liao, Q., Ziyin, L., Gan, Y., Cheung, B., Harnett, M., & Poggio, T. (2024). Self-assembly of a biologically plausible learning circuit. arXiv preprint arXiv:2412.20018.
see this Chat conversation for help;
[https://chatgpt.com/share/6acc41cf-4184-83ec-876f-bddc2db9085c](https://chatgpt.com/share/6acc41cf-4184-83ec-876f-bddc2db9085c)

Note useFBSA=False executes just uses the forward network weights, using a standard backprop algorithm - this should already be implemented (only fix if there is a bug).

Please use the existing FBSAANNpt\_FBSAANNmodel template code provided to define the forward/backward networks; this will need to be extended for your FBSAANN implementation (in particular: the backward and lateral subnetworks, and the connection weight update code have not yet been defined).&#x20;

Exactly the same wrapper code (ANNpt\_\*.py) must be used - this cannot be modified unless a bug is identified. This is important as it enables exact benchmark comparison to other learning algorithms.
